  "notes": "Controlling one's desires and habits, especially regarding food, drink, and lifestyle, for the sake of health. Often used in medical or health-advice contexts.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {節制|せっせい}する: to practice restraint\n- {食事|しょくじ}の{節制|せっせい}: dietary moderation\n- {節制|せっせい}した{生活|せいかつ}: temperate lifestyle\n- {酒|さけ}を{節制|せっせい}する: to moderate one's drinking\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {摂生|せっせい}: taking care of one's health (same pronunciation, often interchangeable)\n- {自制|じせい}: self-control (broader — applies to emotions, impulses, not just health)\n- {我慢|がまん}: endurance, patience (focuses on bearing discomfort)\n\nUSAGE:\n{節制|せっせい} and {摂生|せっせい} are homophones with overlapping meaning. {節制|せっせい} emphasizes cutting back, while {摂生|せっせい} emphasizes healthy living.",
